-- lib/suffix-query.cub — the query of a suffix index, as an interval of the sorted suffixes.
-- A query is a list of tokens. A suffix starts with it (sq-starts) when the query's tokens begin the
-- suffix, each equal by the order, the last of them a prefix of the suffix's token there (so the last
-- word may be typed in part). Over any order with an element top above every element the suffix holds
-- (for bytes, #256 above every byte), the suffixes that start with q are exactly those at least q and
-- not at least sq-up q, which is q with top put after its last token (sq-starts-range). A list of
-- suffixes sorted by lexle therefore holds them as one interval, from the first at least q to the first
-- at least sq-up q (lex-trans), each found by binary search, each comparison Θ(|q|) element
-- comparisons at most.
import "repeats.cub"

